# SRG-APP-000125-WSR-000071  -  CAT II
# The log data and records from the web server must be backed up onto a
# different system or media.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000125-WSR-000071
group:           V-206371
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001348
control_rev5:    AU-9

contribution:    Where the organization uses them, the frozen archive destination
                 (coldToFrozenDir or coldToFrozenScript) and remote store-backed indexes
                 (remotePath) put a copy of the indexed Splunk Web records on other media,
                 and the assessor records which is in use as evidence.

external:        The backup onto different media and its schedule - SPLK-CL-000250 assigns
                 both to the operating system backup tool or another approved tool
external:        Confirmation that the medium is unrelated to the system being logged,
                 which the application cannot establish about a path handed to it

manual_reason:   Splunk Web's records reach the internal indexes, and SPLK-CL-000250 places
                 their backup on "the underlying OS backup tools, or another approved
                 backup tool" with an interview as its check. The application has optional
                 off-instance copy levers but none the authority requires, so no
                 configuration read can decide this requirement without failing a
                 deployment that is backed up as directed.

citation:        coldToFrozenDir non_empty was the only condition, and it fails a stock
                 install for a setting that indexes.conf.spec:792-802 presents as one
                 alternative among several and that the product STIG does not require.
                 Reporting a finding there would charge the application for a backup the
                 benchmark authority itself assigns to an operating system tool.
finding:         No backup of the Splunk Web log records onto a different system or media
                 is in place; the application's optional archive destination is not a
                 substitute for the backup process the requirement names.
